{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"b3cab00338425c0da6d741f037644050ffaa3e47"},"timestamp":1574345240,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU1MjY2MTcwMDE=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3882","origin":"github"},"title":"ENH: Commit message for subdataset installation?","message":"When writing a basic, exemplary YODA-compliant data analysis ([here](http://handbook.datalad.org/en/latest/basics/101-130-yodaproject.html)), I'm making a point of how easily comprehensible a YODA project log can be:\n\n```\nLet’s take a look at the history of the midterm_project analysis dataset:\n\n$ git log --oneline\nc73efce [DATALAD RUNCMD] analyze iris data with classification analysis\n789e6b4 add script for kNN classification and plotting\n9466bd3 [DATALAD] Recorded changes\nab62c74 Apply YODA dataset setup\n8d3c887 [DATALAD] new dataset\n\n“Wow, this is so clean an intuitive!” you congratulate yourself.\n```\n\nWhat is not easily comprehensible from the log however is ``9466bd3 [DATALAD] Recorded changes`` -- this is the installation of a subdataset.\n\nWhat I would like to do is attaching a commit message when installing a subdataset:\n\n```\ndatalad install -d . -s https://github.com/datalad-handbook/iris_data.git input/ -m \"install input data\"\n```\n\nCan you see any adverse effect this could have? I've quickly implemented this in a PR I'll submit shortly (at least locally the tests don't complain) to show what I mean codewise.","files":null}]}